#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:5
#: 35776dbb82744e50acdc49fadad9abed
msgid "Advanced Pixhawk Quadcopter Wiring Chart"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:7
#: c6e333ca4b0c49cabb7acfe565fdc96c
msgid "Jethro Hazelhurst produced this magnificent Pixhawk wiring chart for a Quadcopter for us. (Other autopilots will be wired similarly)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:10
#: f72b2e328c6b4742bcc5f4029a59cf17
msgid "(Control Scroll wheel will let you zoom in on the image below!)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:16
#: 8c85b439d9c541aab8b5f3dfd54cd306
msgid "This chart Illustrates a quadcopter with a variety of options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:18
#: 056173fff4c54a74b6e91e87cdc59579
msgid "A 4 in 1 ESC is used instead of individual ESCs reducing EMF and allowing a neater installation and no power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:20
#: 561755a5262b43369c8e3af6dd7621f8
msgid "Default actual Motor number to Quadcopter frame location is shown below and will require appropriate signal and motor wire routing. The assignment of outputs to motor numbers can be changed by adjusting the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` values for each individual \"x\" output of the autopilot. Note that the AUX1-6 outputs shown below correspond to SERVO9 - SERVO14, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:26
#: 69825ccae918437b9a8a36b7ee6178aa
msgid "A 3DR PPM-Sum encoder with conventional receiver is illustrated. Any ArduPilot compatible receiver can be used. See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for more options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:27
#: 0a767d828ed74992b1c52401c0bb0c8f
msgid "Generally a 3S or 4S LiPo battery is appropriate for a Quadcopter and the XT60 connectors shown are a reliable choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:29
#: be71dddcf8144bdfabe0dedfda826e68
msgid "An optional battery warning indicator can provide quick battery status and provide an audible warning when nearby."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:31
#: 156b27f10cd14826820c96b590b27994
msgid "Optional 3DR telemetry radios may be connected to your autopilot and tablet or laptop to permit real time monitoring and operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:34
#: 1849e8684ec5470cb8b220aa1413618b
msgid "A (GCS (Ground Control Station) program like Mission Planner, AndroPilot or DroidPlanner provides in flight information and control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:38
#: 6e7c75f8627541d588532922d8065a99
msgid "An optional GoPro camera and brushless gimbal are illustrated and can provide very high quality photo and video results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:41
#: 230b8f749f8c4f9ab98901d504625695
msgid "It is quite reasonable to use a GoPro camera and brushless gimbal on 400 and larger Quadcopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:43
#: d84635cf11e248cdb6d055dd0ff369f5
msgid "Brushless camera gimbals perform more smoothly and adequately than the older servo type gimbals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:45
#: 7bc4ab3888ed4c08b7c9250da5258cb4
msgid "The brushless gimbal illustrated above has an anti-vibration mount which is important for good photo results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:47
#: bc96698b5a534816872dad9c4c3603cd
msgid "For cameras larger than GoPro or \"Sport\" types, a larger QuadCopter, HexaCopter or OctoCopter should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:50
#: 4bc71c2b3348439d8f6c258d3b2ce320
msgid "You could also install an optional FPV (First Person View) video system but it is not shown in the illustration above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:53
#: 803dec0920024334aa55eadb32d03338
msgid "An FPV system consists of a tiny video camera and transmitter on the copter plus a receiver and video goggles or an LCD screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:55
#: 84bf49f5b02b4a2c8058a226099f9901
msgid "Almost any size Quadcopter can support a First Person View system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:56
#: 7c7dfbc2e1fe41c4a24b94be1ffbfa23
msgid "An optional OSD (On Screen Display) can add a video heads up display of current in flight conditions to your FPV flight display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-pixhawk-quadcopter-wiring-chart.rst:60
#: 77c5b859378f414f9578e4c2d0cdbf68
msgid "The telemetry, camera, gimbal, FPV and OSD options mentioned above can be combined as you wish for your copter, but start simple."
msgstr ""
